WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.602
Step six is generation from approved evidence.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:11.582
The prompt should clearly separate instructions, policy evidence, structured order facts, and the user's question.

00:00:11.582 --> 00:00:13.403
This reduces ambiguity.

00:00:13.865 --> 00:00:21.140
For example, tell the model to use only the supplied evidence and to say when the evidence is insufficient.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.615
Then provide the policy context with source identifiers.

00:00:25.615 --> 00:00:28.380
Provide the order record separately.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.650
Finally, include the original question.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.155
Why separate these sections?

00:00:34.155 --> 00:00:41.325
Because the model can more easily distinguish instructions from evidence and distinguish general policy from

00:00:41.325 --> 00:00:42.393
customer-specific facts.

00:00:42.843 --> 00:00:49.666
A good prompt does not replace validation, but it creates a cleaner contract for grounded generation.
